From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 06n-arch <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:01:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 37/57] panvk: Fold pass-through geometry shaders into the
 vertex shader (06n-arch)

PanVK has no geometry shaders; 0017 advertises them for DXVK and fails
any pipeline that has one. Unreal Engine 4 games hit that constantly:
UE4 renders into 3D-texture slices (the color grading LUT, the
translucency lighting volume) with a GS that re-emits each triangle
unchanged and only adds gl_Layer. With those draws skipped, the
tonemapper reads an all-zero LUT and the whole 3D view is black while
the HUD, drawn after tonemapping, still shows (Deep Rock Galactic on a
Radxa Orion O6N).

When a GS is compiled together with its VS (monolithic pipelines and
DXVK's pre-rasterization libraries both do that), check whether it is a
pure pass-through: straight-line code, one invocation, stream 0, the
input primitive's vertex count emitted as a strip of the same primitive,
and every output a plain copy of the same vertex's input (gl_Layer and
gl_ViewportIndex may come from vertex 0, which is the provoking one). If
so, make the VS write the GS outputs itself from its own outputs (v10+
has shaderOutputLayer) and compile the GS to an empty stub that binding
ignores and that serializes to just its stage. Anything else still fails
the pipeline as before; the first such GS is printed to stderr so the
matcher can be extended.
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_shader.h    |   3 +
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c | 387 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 387 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

